[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113431,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 68,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lymphadenoma is a benign salivary gland tumour consisting of a proliferation of ductal or sebaceous epithelial cells forming nests within a reactive lymphoid background.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:17:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113432,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 68,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8563/0 Lymphadenoma</p>\r\n<p>8563/0 Sebaceous lymphadenoma</p>\r\n<p>8563/0 Non-sebaceous lymphadenoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:17:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113433,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 68,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2E91.Z &amp; XH7J33 Benign neoplasm of major salivary glands, unspecified &amp; Lymphadenoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:17:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113434,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 68,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:17:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113435,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 68,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Sebaceous lymphadenoma; non-sebaceous lymphadenoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:17:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113436,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 68,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most sebaceous lymphadenomas occur in the parotid/periparotid area or submandibular gland {20032620; 24000514; 33257384}; lacrimal and minor salivary gland tumours have been reported {12076329; 29460186}. Non-sebaceous lymphadenomas frequently occur in parotid gland or periparotid tissue {24944675; 29460186; 32926569}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:17:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113437,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 68,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients present with a slowly growing, painless mass of a few months&rsquo; to several years&rsquo; duration {24944675}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:17:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113438,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 68,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lymphadenomas represent 0.1% of salivary gland neoplasms and &lt;&nbsp;0.5% of salivary gland adenomas {21892186}. The sebaceous type is more common. The patient age range is 10&ndash;78&nbsp;years (median: 59&nbsp;years) {21892186}. Non-sebaceous lymphadenomas tend to affect younger patients, including children {12383217; 18329584; 19138644; 20512641; 23426964}. Sebaceous lymphadenomas have an M:F&nbsp;ratio of 4:3, and non-sebaceous lymphadenomas may show a slight female preference {21892186}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:17:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113439,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 68,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:17:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113440,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 68,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:17:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113441,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 68,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Sebaceous lymphadenomas are slightly larger than non-sebaceous lymphadenomas: 29&nbsp;mm (range: 10&ndash;60&nbsp;mm) and 15&nbsp;mm (range: 6&ndash;50&nbsp;mm), respectively. They are typically well circumscribed to encapsulated, with a grey-white&nbsp;/ tan-yellow solid or multicystic cut surface {29460186}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:17:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113442,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 68,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "<p>Sebaceous lymphadenomas are well circumscribed and variably macrocystic or microcystic. They are composed of variably sized ducts, with foci of sebaceous differentiation in a benign lymphoid background containing reactive lymphoid follicles with germinal centres {12383217; 21892186; 29850339; 32960941}. Pleomorphism and cytological atypia are minimal; necrosis and mitoses are uncommon. Squamous differentiation and oncocytic metaplasia may be seen {16878064; 20032620}. Histiocytes and/or foreign body giant cells, from sebum leakage, are common {12383217; 21892186; 32960941}. Non-sebaceous lymphadenomas are similar but without sebaceous cells {12383217; 21892186; 32960941}.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>Sebocytes stain for p63, EMA, adipophilin, and perilipin. Basal cells are positive for CK5/6 and p63; luminal epithelial cells are positive for CK7, CK18, and CK19 {17431672; 21892186}. Lymphocytes are polytypic. The Ki-67 index is &lt;&nbsp;10%. p16 is positive in sebaceous lymphadenoma; HPV, EBV, and KSHV/HHV8 are negative {21892186}.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>Absence of invasion, extensive epidermoid islands, and <em>MAML2</em> gene rearrangement help to distinguish lymphadenomas from the Warthin-like variant of mucoepidermoid carcinoma {32960941}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-22T14:16:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113443,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 68,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Smears are cellular, showing 3D tissue fragments that may be glandular or solid, composed of bland basaloid or columnar cells, with lymphocytes and histiocytes in a proteinaceous background {19670220; 31967730; 32926569}. Sebaceous differentiation with abundant finely vacuolated microvesicular cytoplasm and central nuclei is not prominent.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:17:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113444,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 68,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not applicable</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:17:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113445,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 68,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> for lymphadenoma, sebaceous subtype: epithelial nests/ducts, sebaceous cells/nests, and a benign lymphoid background; for lymphadenoma, non-sebaceous subtype: epithelial nests/ducts in a benign lymphoid background.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> a well-defined capsule.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:17:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113446,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 68,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not applicable</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:17:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113447,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 68,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are benign tumours, which do not recur if completely excised. Malignant transformation is extremely rare and has been reported in the sebaceous, basaloid, and lymphoid components {12913846; 6704903; 21892186; 31967730}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:17:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]